      <ActivityOrMissionDesc>ZERO8HUNDRED'S MISSION IS TO OFFER COMPASSIONATE, EVIDENCE-BASED SUPPORT TO SERVICE MEMBERS AND THEIR FAMILIES, HELPING THEM NAVIGATE THE UNIQUE CHALLENGES OF TRANSITIONING FROM ACTIVE DUTY TO CIVILIAN LIFE THROUGH A PEER-BASED SOCIAL WORK MODEL. ZERO8HUNDRED TRANSITION SUPPORT ADDRESSES THE NEEDS OF OUR MILITARY TRANSITIONING TO CIVILIAN LIFE BY DELIVERING SERVICES THROUGH A SOCIAL WORK MODEL ZERO8HUNDRED ADDRESSES SUICIDE PREVENTION, EMPLOYMENT, EDUCATION AND BASIC NEEDS. ZERO8HUNDRED DERIVES ITS NAME FROM THE DAILY MILITARY RITUAL OF RAISING THEAMERICAN FLAG AT 0800 8:00AM TO SIGNAL THAT A NEW DAY OF WORK HAS BEGUN. ZERO8HUNDRED PROVIDES A HOLISTIC APPROACH WITH A DIRECT CASE MANAGEMENT SERVICE THAT CONNECTS SERVICE MEMBERS TO SUPPORT 12-18 MONTHS PRIOR TO MILITARY EXIT UPWARDS TO 3 YEARS POST MILITARY SERVICE. ZERO8HUNDRED IS FOCUSED IN THE SOUTHERN CALIFORNIA AREA WITH THE ABILITY TO SUPPORT CLIENTS ACROSS THE STATE OF CALIFORNIA. ZERO8HUNDRED SERVES ALL BRANCHES OF MILITARY SERVI</ActivityOrMissionDesc>
